{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSoBiZ9J1cgiXxVwirzT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ratchet gate is green. Two changes went into lib/ and one worker proposal was rejected; the two gate failures along the way were bugs in my own new assertions, and no existing test was touched.\n\n1. **Warmups D27 \"Monkey Business\" (merged):** I added an Ook! codec to `lib/warmups_codecs.py`: an encoder and decoder plus a `DAYS` entry for day 27. Ook! is just the D26 one-cell Brainfuck written as `Ook? Ook!` token pairs with single spaces. I also added an Ook branch to `lib.decode.decode_chunk`. The encoder reproduces the GM's bytes exactly on the Single, the Time Trial and all 133 Mastery line-27 fragments, and `decode_chunked` gives the confirmed answer on all 133 Mastery sets.\n2. **Metadata D27 \"Packet Loss Prevention\" (merged):** I promoted the existing speculative `pcap.packet_count` extractor to verified. That means a new `lib/meta/pcap.py`, a `_BUILTIN` entry tagged day 27, and removing that key from the speculative `FIELDS`. The `pcapng` spelling stays speculative because only classic pcap was asked. It matches the GM-confirmed counts on 13 of 13 questions (Single 3, Time Trial 32, Mastery 11/11).\n3. **Tests:** I added one check for each of these to `tests/test_day7_fixes.py`. Both failed the first gate run because I'd written them wrong: the wrong Ook ending, and expecting an int where `answer()` returns the string `\"3\"`. I fixed those two new assertions.\n4. **Rejected: the web-double-spent proposal** (make `candidates()` run the double-spend handler alone first). Double Spent was never solved: there's no `confirmed.json` and no submission, only `HELP.md`. The handler it names is an unverified draft that isn't in lib, and the claim that an earlier sequential POST used up the target's only credit is the worker's guess (\"likeliest cause\"), not something the GM confirmed. The risk is still worth checking once a fresh target actually solves.\n5. **Not merged (not D27 GM facts):** the older notes in the scripting and binary solvers are perf ideas carried over from D14–D25. The web-forwarded-misgivings and web-socket-to-me handlers were already in `lib/web/handlers/`, and nothing went into `knowledge.py` or `playbook.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319,"cache_read_input_tokens":75694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":319},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38246abc-afbc-4d01-bb65-9202887e5ea2","uuid":"b4744e90-17ec-4d81-a4bd-924b1a12157a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:10:33.042Z","request_id":"req_011CgSoBiB5ATsoBjxYhKcGY"}
